{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765055,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"CSI-CRCE presents The Double Cross","festival_id":521740,"organization_id":17467,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-30T12:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/csi-crce-presents-the-double-cross-crescendo-fr-crce-students-council-1765055","region":"offline","details":"<h2>THE DOUBLE CROSS &ndash; TWO ROUNDS. ONE HEIST.<\/h2>\n<p><strong>The Double Cross<\/strong> is a two-round technical competition conducted as part of <strong>Crescendo 2026<\/strong>, the annual technical fest of CSI-CRCE. The event combines technical problem-solving, logical reasoning, debugging, deduction and strategic gameplay.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligiblity:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must consist of <strong>1-2 students<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li><strong>CRCE Internal Teams:<\/strong> Both participants must be students of Fr. Conceicao Rodrigues College of Engineering.<\/li>\n<li>Class Limit for CRCE Teams:&nbsp;<strong>2 teams per class<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>External Teams:<\/strong> Students from different colleges can form a team. <strong>Inter-college teams are allowed.<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Inter-specialization\/branch teams are allowed.<\/strong> Participants from different academic specializations\/branches may form a team.<\/li>\n<li>There is no restriction on the combination of specializations within a team, subject to the team eligibility criteria.<\/li>\n<li>The same team will participate in both rounds.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:<\/strong> 29 October 2026<\/li>\n<li><strong>Duration:<\/strong> 2.5 Hours<\/li>\n<li><strong>Time:<\/strong> 10:00 AM &ndash; 12:30 PM<\/li>\n<li><strong>Venue:<\/strong> Rooms 601, 602, 603 &amp; 604<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Teams choose the difficulty of the technical challenge they wish to attempt:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Easy:<\/strong> Correct answer &rarr; movement of 3&ndash;5 spaces<\/li>\n<li><strong>Medium:<\/strong> Correct answer &rarr; movement of 6&ndash;8 spaces<\/li>\n<li><strong>Difficult:<\/strong> Correct answer &rarr; movement of 9&ndash;12 spaces<\/li>\n<li><strong>Incorrect answer:<\/strong> movement of 1&ndash;2 spaces<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Teams interact with Tech Nodes through <strong>Claim Challenges<\/strong> and <strong>Attack Challenges<\/strong>. Technical challenges may involve areas such as programming, logic, debugging, output tracing, binary conversion and logic gates.<\/p>\n<p>There is <strong>no fixed number of questions<\/strong> in Round 1. The number of challenges attempted depends on the progression of each team during the gameplay.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Qualification:<\/strong> The top <strong>3 teams from each of the 4 boards<\/strong> qualify for Round 2, resulting in a maximum of <strong>8 qualifying teams<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Important:<\/strong> Scores from Round 1 will <strong>not<\/strong> be carried forward to Round 2.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:<\/strong> 30 October 2026<\/li>\n<li><strong>Duration:<\/strong> 2 Hours<\/li>\n<li><strong>Time:<\/strong> 10:00 AM &ndash; 12:00 PM<\/li>\n<li><strong>Venue:<\/strong> Rooms 601, 602, 603 &amp; 604<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The qualified teams take part in a digital investigation involving a sequence of interconnected technical and logical challenges.<\/p>\n<p>Each team receives:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Case File<\/li>\n<li>Suspect Profiles<\/li>\n<li>Detective Toolkit<\/li>\n<li>Initial Clue<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must consist of <strong>1-<\/strong><strong>2 participants<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report within the designated check-in time.<\/li>\n<li>Team members must remain together during the event unless instructed otherwise by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>Only the materials, systems and resources explicitly permitted by the organizers may be used.<\/li>\n<li>Sharing answers, clues or solutions with other teams is strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Accessing unauthorized tabs, websites, applications or other resources during the competition is prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Cheating, unauthorized assistance, tampering with the competition system or attempting to gain an unfair advantage may result in immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Any disruptive or inappropriate conduct towards participants, volunteers, organizers or staff may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must follow all instructions given by the event coordinators.<\/li>\n<li>Organizers reserve the right to investigate suspected violations of the rules.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the <strong>Organizing Committee will be final and binding<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Round 2 will begin with a <strong>fresh score<\/strong>, and Round 1 scores will not be carried forward.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>Winner:<\/h2>\n<p>For <strong>Round 1<\/strong>, teams are ranked primarily based on the <strong>number of technical challenges solved correctly<\/strong>. In case of a tie, the following criteria are applied successively:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Accuracy<\/li>\n<li>Time Taken<\/li>\n<li>Tech Cash<\/li>\n<li>Tech Nodes Owned<\/li>\n<li>Tech Networks Owned<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Winners receive cash prizes, exclusive goodies, and recognition for their performance.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33503862,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-02T23:21:16+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T23:07:34+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"FR6BwLm","hasht